---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NeuralNetwork from '../NeuralNetwork.astro';
import type { Locale } from '../../i18n/ui';
import { useTranslations } from '../../i18n/utils';

export interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}
const { locale } = Astro.props;
const t = useTranslations(locale);
---

<Layout
  title={t('pageTitles.about')}
  description={t('pageTitles.aboutDescription')}
  active="about"
  locale={locale}
>
  <!-- ═══════════════ HERO ═════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="section-glow lilac" style="top:-50px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%)"></div>
    <div class="section-glow blue" style="bottom:0;right:-100px"></div>
    <NeuralNetwork color="lilac" density="medium" opacity={0.30} />
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-hero-inner fi">
        <div style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:24px"><span class="label" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><span style="width:20px;height:1px;background:var(--grad);display:block"></span>About D.Lab Experts</span></div>
        <h1 class="about-hero-title">Research Hub.<br /><span class="gradient-text">Vanguard posture.</span></h1>
        <p class="about-hero-sub">D.Lab Experts is a research hub in applied intelligence and cybersecurity. We research, test and publish as proof of method, so that boards, founders and operators can decide with grounding in a world that has moved past its own defenses.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="atom-container fi d1">
        <div class="atom">
          <div class="atom-glow"></div>
          <div class="atom-nucleus"></div>
          <div class="atom-orbit atom-orbit-1">
            <div class="atom-orbit-wrap atom-orbit-wrap-1">
              <div class="atom-orbit-ring"></div>
              <div class="atom-electron atom-electron-1"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="atom-orbit atom-orbit-2">
            <div class="atom-orbit-wrap atom-orbit-wrap-2">
              <div class="atom-orbit-ring"></div>
              <div class="atom-electron atom-electron-2"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="atom-orbit atom-orbit-3">
            <div class="atom-orbit-wrap atom-orbit-wrap-3">
              <div class="atom-orbit-ring"></div>
              <div class="atom-electron atom-electron-3"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-stats fi d2">
        <div class="about-stat">
          <div class="about-stat-val" style="color:var(--lilac)">$ 4.4T</div>
          <div class="about-stat-lbl">AI &amp; data market by 2030 (IDC)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-stat">
          <div class="about-stat-val" style="color:var(--blue)">73%</div>
          <div class="about-stat-lbl">of SMBs decide without data (SEBRAE, 2023)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-stat">
          <div class="about-stat-val" style="color:var(--cyan)">$ 4.88M</div>
          <div class="about-stat-lbl">Average cost of a data breach (IBM, 2024)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-stat">
          <div class="about-stat-val" style="color:var(--green)">Dual</div>
          <div class="about-stat-lbl">Intelligence &amp; cyber in the same operation</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-sep"></div>

  <!-- ═══════════════ QUEM SOMOS ════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-glow lilac" style="top:30%;left:-120px"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-split fi">
        <aside class="about-split-aside">
          <div class="about-split-eyebrow">Who we are</div>
          <h2>What D.Lab Experts is</h2>
          <p class="lead">A <strong style="color:var(--white)">Research Hub</strong> treating <strong style="color:var(--white)">data intelligence</strong> and <strong style="color:var(--white)">cybersecurity</strong> as the same problem: understand before the move, protect after it. We research, publish, and when the context calls for it, translate the same methodology into consulting engagements under NDA.</p>
          <div class="aside-stats">
            <div class="aside-stat">
              <div class="aside-stat-val" style="color:var(--lilac)">73%</div>
              <div class="aside-stat-lbl">of SMB managers decide by intuition<br />SEBRAE, 2023</div>
            </div>
            <div class="aside-stat">
              <div class="aside-stat-val" style="color:var(--blue)">23×</div>
              <div class="aside-stat-lbl">more customers at data-driven companies<br />McKinsey Global Institute</div>
            </div>
            <div class="aside-stat">
              <div class="aside-stat-val" style="color:var(--cyan)">$ 4.88M</div>
              <div class="aside-stat-lbl">average cost of a data breach<br />IBM, 2024</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
        <div class="about-split-content">
          <p>D.Lab Experts was born from a documented premise. According to SEBRAE (2023), <strong>73% of SMB managers make critical decisions by intuition</strong>. In parallel, LLMs and agents accelerate execution while multiplying attack surfaces, and the global average cost of a data breach is <strong>$4.88 million</strong> (IBM, 2024). Blind decisions and exposed operations are two sides of the same problem.</p>
          <p>On the intelligence side, we cross-reference public sources, APIs, scraping and primary research to answer what stalls decisions for boards, founders and operators. The global data analytics market grows 13.5% per year (Statista, 2024), and data-driven companies are <strong>23 times more likely to acquire customers</strong> (McKinsey Global Institute).</p>
          <div class="split-insight">
            Accumulated data is noise. What turns scattered data into an actionable decision is the <strong>interpretation architecture</strong> behind it.
            <span class="src">D.Lab Experts · Research Hub, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p>On the cyber side, we run intrusion tests, map vulnerabilities and investigate the new surfaces AI and automation have opened. Ransomware attacks grew 73% globally year over year (Statista, 2024), and over 80% of organizations experienced at least one breach in the last 12 months. With autonomous agents in operation, the window only gets shorter.</p>
          <p>We publish the method. Open analysis as proof of how we think. Work under NDA becomes a consulting engagement when someone needs the same rigor applied to their own context. The rest is noise.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-sep"></div>

  <!-- ═══════════════ O QUE FAZEMOS ════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-glow blue" style="top:20%;right:-100px"></div>
    <div class="section-glow cyan" style="bottom:10%;left:-80px"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-section-header fi">
        <div class="eyebrow">Hub scope</div>
        <h2>What we research</h2>
        <p class="lead">Two practices that inform each other. Intelligence shows where to move; security ensures the move survives. Each runs in two modes: open publication (Research Hub) and closed engagement (consulting under NDA).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="services-split">
        <div class="service-card data fi-l d1">
          <div class="service-card-icon lilac">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22" fill="none"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="2" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="12" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="2" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="3" y="12" width="7" height="7" rx="2" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M15.5 12v7M12 15.5h7" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Applied Intelligence</h3>
          <p>Companies using advanced analytics generate <strong>126% more profit</strong> than peers (Bain &amp; Company). The Hub researches what generic models miss: markets, behavior, competition, AI foresight. We publish open methodology, and when a project arises, the same protocol serves the closed context.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Strategic analysis and market sizing</li>
            <li>Competitive intelligence and benchmarking</li>
            <li>Audience profiling and demand analysis</li>
            <li>Tech foresight: AI, agents and LLMs in operation</li>
            <li>Responsible AI and automation adoption</li>
            <li>Politics, public opinion and regulatory movement</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card cyber fi-r d1">
          <div class="service-card-icon cyan">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22" fill="none"><path d="M11 2L4 5.5v5c0 4.7 3 8.5 7 10 4-1.5 7-5.3 7-10v-5L11 2z" stroke="url(#g-green)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M8 11l2.5 2.5L14.5 9" stroke="url(#g-green)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Cybersecurity</h3>
          <p>Cybercrime is projected to cost <strong>$10.5 trillion per year globally by 2025</strong> (Cybersecurity Ventures). We investigate modern attack surfaces, including those AI and autonomous agents have just opened, and translate the findings into defensive posture before the cost becomes a headline.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Pentest across web, mobile and infrastructure</li>
            <li>Vulnerability analysis and risk classification</li>
            <li>LLM security and assessment of agents in operation</li>
            <li>Compliance with GDPR, ISO 27001, NIST and LGPD</li>
            <li>Monitoring and incident response</li>
            <li>Team training and security awareness</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-sep"></div>

  <!-- ═══════════════ COMO OPERAMOS ════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-glow lilac" style="top:50%;right:-100px"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-section-header fi">
        <div class="eyebrow">Methodology</div>
        <h2>How we operate</h2>
        <p class="lead">One protocol, four stages, from question to delivery. Four pillars run through every stage. None are negotiable.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="method-steps fi d1">
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">01</div>
          <div class="method-step-title">Briefing</div>
          <div class="method-step-desc">We frame the context, the hypothesis and the decision criteria, or the risk perimeter to map.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">02</div>
          <div class="method-step-title">Collection &amp; Modeling</div>
          <div class="method-step-desc">We cross-reference multiple data sources, or run the security tests with a defined scope.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">03</div>
          <div class="method-step-title">Synthesis</div>
          <div class="method-step-desc">Raw data turned into structured insights with scores, classifications and visualizations.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">04</div>
          <div class="method-step-title">Delivery</div>
          <div class="method-step-desc">Full report with a clear recommendation, prioritized action plan and an interpretation call.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pillars-grid fi">
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 2L12.5 7.5H18L13.5 11L15.5 17L10 13.5L4.5 17L6.5 11L2 7.5H7.5L10 2Z" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div>
          <div class="pillar-title">Methodological rigor</div>
          <div class="pillar-desc">Every analysis with documented, replicable, transparent methodology.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1.2"/><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="3" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1.2"/><path d="M10 3v2M10 15v2M3 10h2M15 10h2" stroke="url(#g1)" stroke-width="1" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div>
          <div class="pillar-title">Primary data</div>
          <div class="pillar-desc">Our own collection when open sources are not enough for the decision.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M3 15l4-4 3 2.5 4-5.5 3-2" stroke="url(#g-green)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div>
          <div class="pillar-title">Reasoning exposed</div>
          <div class="pillar-desc">You see exactly how we arrived at the recommendation or the diagnosis.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 2L4 5.5v5c0 4 2.5 7.2 6 8.5 3.5-1.3 6-4.5 6-8.5v-5L10 2z" stroke="url(#g-green)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M7.5 10l2 2 3.5-4" stroke="url(#g-green)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div>
          <div class="pillar-title">Independence</div>
          <div class="pillar-desc">No bias. We report what the data shows and what the tests reveal.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-sep"></div>

  <!-- ═══════════════ POR QUE AGORA ════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-glow cyan" style="top:30%;left:-80px"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-split fi">
        <aside class="about-split-aside">
          <div class="about-split-eyebrow">The landscape</div>
          <h2>Why this matters <span class="gradient-text">now</span></h2>
          <p class="lead">The window for strategic decisions has never been narrower. The cost of getting it wrong, in markets or in security, is documented and only growing.</p>
          <div class="aside-stats">
            <div class="aside-stat">
              <div class="aside-stat-val" style="color:var(--lilac)">29%</div>
              <div class="aside-stat-lbl">of new businesses fail in year one<br />Bureau of Labor Statistics</div>
            </div>
            <div class="aside-stat">
              <div class="aside-stat-val" style="color:var(--cyan)">+72%</div>
              <div class="aside-stat-lbl">global ransomware attack growth YoY<br />Statista, 2024</div>
            </div>
            <div class="aside-stat">
              <div class="aside-stat-val" style="color:var(--green)">$ 33B</div>
              <div class="aside-stat-lbl">Business Intelligence market by 2027<br />Mordor Intelligence</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
        <div class="about-split-content">
          <p>The landscape demands action. <strong>29% of new businesses fail in their first year</strong> and 50% before year five. The main cause isn't lack of capital. It's lack of information to decide.</p>
          <p>At the same time, ransomware attacks grew <strong>72% globally year over year</strong> (Statista, 2024), and regulators have applied fines reaching tens of millions of dollars. The boom of LLMs and autonomous agents only worsens the math: faster execution and newly exposed surfaces at the same time.</p>
          <div class="split-insight">
            Companies that adopt a data-driven culture see <strong>5 to 8% more productivity and 6% more profitability</strong> than their peers.
            <span class="src">Harvard Business Review</span>
          </div>
          <p>On the upside, the numbers show opportunity. The Business Intelligence market should reach <strong>$33 billion by 2027</strong> (Mordor Intelligence). Whoever moves with a solid context read captures compound advantage over those who wait for the competitor to go first.</p>
          <p>D.Lab Experts exists to close that gap. Open research that grounds the move. Offensive security operation that survives the next attempt. <strong>Documented method instead of prose.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-sep"></div>

  <!-- ═══════════════ CTA ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="about-cta">
    <div class="section-glow lilac" style="top:50%;left:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%)"></div>
    <div class="container fi">
      <h2>Research that grounds the move.<br />Operation that <span class="gradient-text">survives the next attempt.</span></h2>
      <p>Research Hub first. Consulting when the context calls for it. Start with the open publications, or talk to us directly.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <a href="/blog" class="btn btn-primary">Read open publications →</a>
        <a href="/contato" class="btn btn-ghost">Talk about a project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
